    "items": [
     {
      "pClass": "productdescription",
      "pText": "Fugadi is a revolving play pole named after fugdi, the spinning game played in Maharashtra and Goa. A tall pole in Play Red and Baby Blue carries four handgrips on ropes near the top. Children hold a grip each and move round the pole in rhythm, almost like a dance, instead of sitting on a spinning seat. It is designed for ages 5 to 12, and the game works for boys and girls alike. Revolving and balancing build arm strength, spatial awareness and balance. The pole stands on a round black base and takes very little ground. It belongs to our Timeless Play collection. The galvanised pipe and roto-moulded parts carry our 3-year warranty. Ask us how much clear space to allow around it."
     }
    ]
   }
